2186420503 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420498 13194139534393 17592186045417 true] [17592186420503 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420499 13194139534393 17592186045417 true] [17592186420503 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420500 13194139534393 17592186045417 true] [17592186420503 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420501 13194139534393 17592186045417 true] [17592186420503 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420502 13194139534393 17592186045417 true] [17592186420503 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534393 17592186045417 true] [17592186420503 1077 "selection" 13194139534393 17592186045417 true] [17592186420503 1078 #edb/ref 17592186420500 13194139534393 17592186045417 true] [17592186420503 1079 #uuid "236e449f-8bdf-5cb7-898e-9834bb6e7cf6" 13194139534393 17592186045417 true] [17592186420504 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420503 13194139534393 17592186045417 true] [17592186420504 1069 "q-37456" 13194139534393 17592186045417 true] [17592186420504 1071 "The function \n$f(x,y)$ \nhas the second derivative\n\n$$\n\\boldsymbol{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nand has a stationary point at $(1,1).$ If $H$ denotes the Hessian determinant of $f,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $H(1,1)>0$\n\nII. $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(1,1)>0$\n\nIII. The point $(1,1)$ is a local minimum of $f$" 13194139534393 17592186045417 true] [17592186420504 1072 #uuid "d1a7556c-36af-5f0b-b64c-a00089e6850e" 13194139534393 17592186045417 true] [17592186420504 1074 "The second partial derivative test states that if $a\\in {R}^{2}$ is a stationary point of $f(x,y)$ with Hessian determinant $H(a),$ we have the following:\n\n- If $H(a)>0,$ then:\n\n- if $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(a)<0,$ then $f$ has a local maximum at $a$\n\n- if $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(a)>0,$ then $f$ has a local minimum at $a$\n\n- If $H(a)<0,$ then $f$ has a saddle point at $a$\n\n- If $H(a)=0,$ then the second partial derivatives test is inconclusive.\n\nEvaluating the second derivative at $(1,1),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(1,1)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed, computing the determinant of ${f}^{″}(1,1),$ we get\n\n$$\nH(1,1)=det({f}^{″}(1,1))=2\\cdot 0-{1}^{2}=-1<0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, we have $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(1,1)=({f}^{″}(1,1))_{11}=2>0.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $H(1,1)<0,$ then $(1,1)$ is a saddle point by the second partial derivative test.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139534393 17592186045417 true] [17592186420505 1062 #uuid "0cb8913a-c24a-569b-b341-a73bcd973a28" 13194139534393 17592186045417 true] [17592186420505 1063 #edb/ref 17592186371555 13194139534393 17592186045417 true] [17592186420506 1062 #uuid "0f371a43-edc5-5d80-a3b1-085b4b459f8e" 13194139534393 17592186045417 true] [17592186420506 1063 #edb/ref 17592186411864 13194139534393 17592186045417 true] [17592186420507 1062 #uuid "11063da2-ce8c-5020-9054-aada599f4c10" 13194139534393 17592186045417 true] [17592186420507 1063 #edb/ref 17592186411872 13194139534393 17592186045417 true] [17592186420508 1062 #uuid "1111550a-442b-5be1-b20f-bc6bd15e780f" 13194139534393 17592186045417 true] [17592186420508 1063 #edb/ref 17592186284536 13194139534393 17592186045417 true] [17592186420509 1062 #uuid "12cb7b91-cb76-51c5-ab5b-7c44ffdfba80" 13194139534393 17592186045417 true] [17592186420509 1063 #edb/ref 17592186411871 13194139534393 17592186045417 true] [17592186420510 1062 #uuid "13847332-d99e-501c-ab44-70f840f773c0" 13194139534393 17592186045417 true] [17592186420510 1063 #edb/ref 17592186308728 13194139534393 17592186045417 true] [17592186420511 1062 #uuid "148ce9d4-ffa2-5ec2-88c2-a995285a017c" 13194139534393 17592186045417 true] [17592186420511 1063 #edb/ref 17592186411873 13194139534393 17592186045417 true] [17592186420512 1062 #uuid "2353488d-1c48-5933-ba8a-72e400e13ae2" 13194139534393 17592186045417 true] [17592186420512 1063 #edb/ref 17592186411856